      "writtenOn": "2026-10-24T00:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I discussed this with the reviewer (tkjos@), and his proposal was to introduce a separate wrapper interface that uses a different callback signature. Since our callback needs almost none of the context in `vfio_platform_device`, this should be fine for us.\n\nThis new registration handler will have to use some internal callback that matches the existing `vfio_platform_reset_fn_t` signature, which is responsible for calling the user-provided handler, passing it the more generic device info (perhaps just `struct device` as you\u0027ve proposed here).\n\nSee b/577252424 for more detail. I believe this proposed new interface will make this change and b/526875176 obsolete, since it\u0027s been determined exposing this much of VFIO in the KMI is unacceptable.",
